      {
        "id": "thm-rpm-finite-future-momentum-sum",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Finite causal sums and center-of-momentum rest observer",
        "statement": "Let $(A,V,\\eta,C^+)$ be the oriented time-oriented affine Minkowski model with $c>0$, and fix an inertial frame. For a finite nonempty list $P_1,\\ldots,P_N$ of nonzero future-causal vectors in $V$, let $Q:=\\sum_{i=1}^N P_i$, let $m_i:=\\sqrt{-\\eta(P_i,P_i)}/c$ (so $m_i=0$ exactly for a null leg), and let $M(Q)$ be the invariant mass of the total when $Q$ is timelike, as defined in [[def-sr-total-four-momentum-and-invariant-mass]].\n\nThen $Q$ is nonzero and future causal. If at least one $P_i$ is timelike, then $Q$ is future timelike. If all $P_i$ are null, then $Q$ is null exactly when all $P_i$ lie on the same future null ray; otherwise $Q$ is future timelike. Whenever $Q$ is timelike, the center-of-momentum frame exists, its time-axis observer $n_Q=Q/(M(Q)c)$ has zero total spatial momentum and total observer energy $M(Q)c^2$, and\n\n$$M(Q)\\ge\\sum_{i=1}^N m_i.$$\n\nEquality holds exactly when every $P_i$ is massive and there is one future unit timelike vector $n$ such that $P_i=m_i c\\,n$ for every $i$. A nonzero future-null total has no center-of-momentum frame.",
        "deps": [
          "def-sr-total-four-momentum-and-invariant-mass",
          "def-sr-observed-energy-momentum-and-kinetic-energy",
          "def-inertial-frame-and-inertial-chart",
          "lem-sr-future-causal-sums-and-inertial-coordinate-criterion",
          "lem-sr-center-of-momentum-frame",
          "lem-sr-energy-momentum-observer-identities",
          "thm-cauchy-schwarz-finite"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-sr-total-four-momentum-and-invariant-mass": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-sr-observed-energy-momentum-and-kinetic-energy": "mathematical-premise",
