      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-two-body-com-kinematics",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Complete two-body rest-frame kinematics",
        "statement": "Let a finite isolated collision have future-timelike total $Q$ of invariant mass $M>0$, and set $W:=Mc^2$. Suppose the complete outgoing list consists of exactly two legs, with recorded rest masses $a,b\\ge0$; by the adopted balance postulate, their four-momenta must sum to $Q$. In a center-of-momentum frame with time-axis observer $n_Q$, a nonzero two-product state with $\\mathbf p_a+\\mathbf p_b=0$ exists exactly when\n\n$$W\\ge(a+b)c^2\\quad\\hbox{if }a,b>0,\\qquad W>(a+b)c^2\\quad\\hbox{if }a=0\\hbox{ or }b=0.$$\n\nWhen it exists, there are $k\\ge0$ and a unit vector $\\mathbf e\\in n_Q^\\perp$ such that $\\mathbf p_a=k\\mathbf e$ and $\\mathbf p_b=-k\\mathbf e$. The energies and momentum magnitude are\n\n$$E_a=\\frac{W^2+(a^2-b^2)c^4}{2W},\\qquad E_b=\\frac{W^2+(b^2-a^2)c^4}{2W},\\qquad k^2=\\frac{[W^2-(a+b)^2c^4][W^2-(a-b)^2c^4]}{4W^2c^2}.$$\n\nFor $a,b>0$ at threshold, $k=0$ and the direction is immaterial. If a massless product is present, the strict threshold is required because a zero momentum would be the forbidden zero four-vector. These equations describe kinematic balance only. In SI units $a,b,M$ are kilograms, $W,E_a,E_b$ are joules, and $k$ is kilogram metres per second; the norm and dot product on $n_Q^\\perp$ are induced by $\\eta$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-collision-objects",
          "post-rpm-isolated-collision-balance",
          "pthm-rpm-system-mass-threshold",
          "pthm-rpm-inverse-momentum-and-work",
          "lem-sr-center-of-momentum-frame",
          "lem-sr-future-causal-sums-and-inertial-coordinate-criterion",
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy"
        ],
