        "id": "pthm-rpm-kinematic-elastic-channel",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Elastic channel momentum magnitude and direction freedom",
        "statement": "Consider a two-product elastic channel in a finite isolated collision: the complete incoming and outgoing lists each have exactly two legs, their recorded rest masses agree pairwise, the total four-momentum is timelike, and the balance postulate is adopted. In the center-of-momentum frame, let the incoming momenta be $k\\mathbf e_{\\rm in}$ and $-k\\mathbf e_{\\rm in}$ in the spatial rest space $n_Q^\\perp$, where $k\\ge0$ is fixed by [[pthm-rpm-two-body-com-kinematics]]. Every admissible outgoing pair has the same momentum magnitude $k$. If $k>0$, any unit vector $\\mathbf e_{\\rm out}\\in n_Q^\\perp$ gives an on-shell outgoing pair $k\\mathbf e_{\\rm out},-k\\mathbf e_{\\rm out}$ with the same total four-momentum; thus kinematics alone leaves the full direction sphere available. If $k=0$, both products are at rest and the direction is undefined. No isotropic or uniform distribution of directions follows.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-collision-objects",
          "post-rpm-isolated-collision-balance",
          "pthm-rpm-two-body-com-kinematics",
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy"
