        "id": "texp-rpm-ideal-fusion-mass",
        "kind": "thought-experiment",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Ideal two-particle fusion and internal mass",
        "statement": "In a hypothetical isolated event, let two massive particles of equal rest mass $m>0$ have opposite velocities $\\mathbf v$ and $-\\mathbf v$ in one inertial laboratory, with $|\\mathbf v|<c$ and $\\gamma=(1-|\\mathbf v|^2/c^2)^{-1/2}$. Suppose, as a stipulated possible channel, that they form one massive product at rest in that laboratory and that there are no other incoming or outgoing legs. Conditional on the balance postulate, the product rest mass is\n\n$$M=2m\\gamma,$$\n\nso its excess rest mass over the two incoming rest masses is $2m(\\gamma-1)$, and the corresponding rest-energy increase is $2m(\\gamma-1)c^2$. This equals the incoming kinetic energy in the specified laboratory. When $\\mathbf v=0$, the excess is zero. The item does not assert that such a perfectly complete fusion channel occurs in nature.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-collision-objects",
          "post-rpm-isolated-collision-balance",
